**Date:** 8 November 2026 · **Author:** OpenCode harness for piotter121

## Context

The export's [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is an accepted historical record;
it has not been edited. Its subject-only rule contradicts the executable classifier and mixes distinct
problems in [incident 4471](/kb/incidents/4471-review). Similar words are not evidence of a shared cause.

## Replacement rule for this review

1. Deduplicate export rows by report ID, keeping the last occurrence as the supplied code does.
2. Look up the tenant's locale and booking form; read the channel and report body.
3. Use the executable cause rule to propose a group, then check that the symptom fits it.
4. Merge only when evidence supports the same cause. Subject similarity is a search aid, not a merge test.
5. Keep unknown tenants and contradictory symptoms visible for investigation, rather than treating null causes as matches.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

The desk must read more context, but engineers get one problem per ticket. Different subjects may merge;
identical subjects may stay separate. Keep a count and report-ID membership for each cause without double counting.
Do not silently rewrite an accepted decision: a new record documents what replaces it and why.
This proposal does not claim the live support desk has approved or adopted the new rule.

